.TH GOLEM-CHECK 1 2026-11-03 golem-team-shield "User Commands"
.SH NAME
golem-check \- report the AI coding agent settings that let agents act without asking
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B golem-check
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B golem-check \-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B golem-check
reads the settings of the AI coding agents on this machine and prints the ones
that let an agent act without asking, worst first: permission prompts turned
off, every command allowed, every folder trusted, and no sandbox.
.PP
It reads Claude Code (including its managed settings and MDM profiles),
Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI, Devin, and the VS Code family of editors (VS Code,
VS Code Insiders, VSCodium, Cursor, Windsurf, Antigravity), and the settings of
each repository Claude Code has opened.
.PP
It reads files and nothing else, and sends nothing anywhere.
It reports a setting's name and value, never a file's contents.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-json
Print every finding, informational ones included, as JSON: a list of objects
with
.BR client ,
.BR check ,
.B severity
.RB ( dangerous ,
.B suspicious
or
.BR info ),
.BR scope ,
.BR location ,
.BR setting ,
.B value
and
.BR detail .
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the report was written, whatever it found; 1 when it could not be
written; 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR golem\-exec (1)
.PP
https://github.com/GolemTeam/golem-team-shield
